{
  "title": "Glomus Tumor",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pathology/8075/glomus-tumor",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 22 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Glomus Tumors are rare benign tumors of the glomus body, often occurring in the subungual region.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "The condition is typically seen in patients between the ages of 20 and 40 who present with a painful subungal mass with bluish discoloration.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made with a biopsy showing a well-defined lesion lacking cellular atypia or mitotic activity with the presence of small round cells with dark nuclei.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is usually marginal excision**.**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "occurs in patients 20 to 40 years of age",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anatomic ocation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "75% occur in hand",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "50% are subungual",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "50% have erosions of distal phalanx (primary involvement of bone being very rare)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "less common locations: palm, wrist, forearm, foot",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Forms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may involve either the soft tissue and/or bone",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Frequently associated with a delay in diagnosis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Glomus body",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**the glomus body is a perivascular temperature regulating structure** frequently located at the tip of a digit or beneath the nail",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms (classic triad)",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "paroxysmal pain",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "exquisite tenderness to touch",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**cold intolerance**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "small bluish nodule",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "often difficult to see, especially in the subungual location",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**nail ridging or discoloration is common**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "Love test",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "pressure to the area with a pinhead elicits exquisite pain",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "100% sensitive, 78% accurate",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "Hildreth test",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "tourniquet inflation reduces pain/tenderness and abolishes tenderness to the Love test",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "92% sensitive, 91% specific",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "glomus tumors can produce a pressure erosion of the underlying bone and an associated **deformity of the bone cortex**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8075/images/glomus%20erosion%20into%20distal%20phalanx.jpg",
                  "caption": "Glomus tumor eroding into the distal phalanx"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "helpful to establish diagnosis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "present as a low T1 signal and high T2 signal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8075/images/glomus%20mri.jpg",
                  "caption": "glomus tumor T2 MRI showing bright signal"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Histology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "well-defined lesion lacking cellular atypia or mitotic activity",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8075/images/glomus_tumor%20histology.jpg",
                  "caption": "glomus tumor low power"
                }
              ],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "small round cells with dark nuclei",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [
                    {
                      "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/8075/images/glomus%20tumor%20high%20power.jpg",
                      "caption": "glomus tumor high power histology slide"
                    }
                  ],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "associated small vessels in a hyaline/myxoid stroma",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "can show **gland-like or nest structures, separated by stromal elements**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "marginal excision is curative",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "symptoms affecting quality of life",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "due to the benign nature of this disease, recurrence is uncommon",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "several cases of malignant glomus tumors have been reported in the literature",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "reconstruction of nail bed contour with autologous fat graft",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "for large defects after resection",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "1",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Recurrence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "20%",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
